      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Ch3 data-start=\u002294\u0022 data-end=\u0022127\u0022 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong data-start=\u002298\u0022 data-end=\u0022127\u0022\u003EHow To Get A Bigger Squat\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u0022129\u0022 data-end=\u0022400\u0022 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003EIf you want to put more weight on the bar and build powerful legs, it\u2019s not just about squatting more often. A bigger squat comes from strengthening all the muscles that support the movement \u2014 your quads, hips, and core. Here\u2019s how to target each one for maximum gains.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u0022402\u0022 data-end=\u0022744\u0022 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong data-start=\u0022402\u0022 data-end=\u0022425\u0022\u003E1. Train Your Quads\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EYour quadriceps are the primary movers in the squat, especially in the bottom half of the lift. Strengthen them with \u003Cstrong data-start=\u0022545\u0022 data-end=\u0022563\u0022\u003Eleg extensions\u003C/strong\u003E to build isolated quad power and \u003Cstrong data-start=\u0022597\u0022 data-end=\u0022612\u0022\u003Ehack squats\u003C/strong\u003E to mimic the squat pattern with added stability. These exercises help you drive out of the hole with more confidence and control.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u0022746\u0022 data-end=\u00221069\u0022 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong data-start=\u0022746\u0022 data-end=\u0022777\u0022\u003E2. Train Your Hip Extensors\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EYour glutes and hamstrings play a huge role in locking out the squat. Incorporate \u003Cstrong data-start=\u0022862\u0022 data-end=\u0022877\u0022\u003Ehip thrusts\u003C/strong\u003E to develop explosive hip drive and \u003Cstrong data-start=\u0022913\u0022 data-end=\u0022939\u0022\u003EBulgarian split squats\u003C/strong\u003E to build strength and balance in each leg individually. Strong hip extensors translate to a smoother and stronger squat ascent.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u00221071\u0022 data-end=\u00221322\u0022 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong data-start=\u00221071\u0022 data-end=\u00221093\u0022\u003E3. Train Your Core\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EA strong core keeps you stable and upright under heavy weight. Add \u003Cstrong data-start=\u00221163\u0022 data-end=\u00221184\u0022\u003Eab-wheel rollouts\u003C/strong\u003E and \u003Cstrong data-start=\u00221189\u0022 data-end=\u00221211\u0022\u003Ehanging leg raises\u003C/strong\u003E to your routine to build the kind of midsection strength that prevents collapse and improves power transfer.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u00221324\u0022 data-end=\u00221458\u0022 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003EBy strengthening each of these key areas, you\u2019ll not only lift heavier \u2014 you\u2019ll squat more efficiently, safely, and with confidence.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
      <Value Culture="sv"><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Ch3 data-start=\u002294\u0022 data-end=\u0022127\u0022 data-pm-slice=\u00221 1 []\u0022 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong data-start=\u002298\u0022 data-end=\u0022127\u0022\u003EHur Du Blir B\u00E4ttre P\u00E5 Kn\u00E4b\u00F6j\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOm du vill l\u00E4gga mer vikt p\u00E5 st\u00E5ngen och bygga kraftfulla ben handlar det inte bara om att b\u00F6ja oftare. En st\u00F6rre kn\u00E4b\u00F6j kommer fr\u00E5n att st\u00E4rka alla muskler som st\u00F6der r\u00F6relsen \u2013 dina quadriceps, h\u00F6fter och b\u00E5l. H\u00E4r \u00E4r hur du tr\u00E4nar varje del f\u00F6r maximala resultat.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Col data-start=\u0022437\u0022 data-end=\u00221430\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u0022440\u0022 data-end=\u0022810\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ETr\u00E4na dina fr\u00E4mre l\u00E5rmuskler\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EDina quadriceps \u00E4r de prim\u00E4ra musklerna i kn\u00E4b\u00F6jen, s\u00E4rskilt i den nedre halvan av r\u00F6relsen. St\u00E4rk dem med benspark f\u00F6r att bygga isolerad styrka i framsida l\u00E5r och hack squats f\u00F6r att efterlikna kn\u00E4b\u00F6jsr\u00F6relsen med extra stabilitet. Dessa \u00F6vningar hj\u00E4lper dig att driva upp ur bottenl\u00E4get med mer kontroll och sj\u00E4lvf\u00F6rtroende.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u0022815\u0022 data-end=\u00221173\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ETr\u00E4na din rumpa\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EDina s\u00E4tesmuskler och hamstrings spelar en avg\u00F6rande roll i att l\u00E5sa ut kn\u00E4b\u00F6jen. Inkludera hip thrusts f\u00F6r att utveckla explosiv h\u00F6ftkraft och bulgariska split squats f\u00F6r att bygga styrka och balans i varje ben individuellt. Starka h\u00F6ftstr\u00E4ckare leder till en j\u00E4mnare och starkare uppresning i kn\u00E4b\u00F6jen.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u00221178\u0022 data-end=\u00221430\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ETr\u00E4na din b\u00E5l\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EEn stark b\u00E5l h\u00E5ller dig stabil och uppr\u00E4tt under tunga vikter. L\u00E4gg till ab-wheel rollouts och h\u00E4ngande benlyft i ditt program f\u00F6r att bygga den typ av b\u00E5lstyrka som f\u00F6rhindrar kollaps och f\u00F6rb\u00E4ttrar kraft\u00F6verf\u00F6ringen.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ol\u003E\u003Cp data-start=\u00221432\u0022 data-end=\u00221601\u0022 data-is-last-node=\u0022\u0022 data-is-only-node=\u0022\u0022\u003EGenom att st\u00E4rka var och en av dessa nyckelomr\u00E5den kommer du inte bara att lyfta tyngre \u2013 du kommer ocks\u00E5 att b\u00F6ja mer effektivt, s\u00E4krare och med st\u00F6rre sj\u00E4lvf\u00F6rtroende.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </pageContent>
